-- A derived-row template too deep to publish is reported, not
-- published as a silent `<error>`. `A.eq` needs `a.foo` at a method type
-- 509 tuples deep, which A's own writer and every reader accept. `B.W`'s
-- derived `eq` row wraps that requirement in two more levels, past the
-- writer's 512. `Facts.templateScheme` must go through the one publication
-- routine — its `hasError` scan, and `noteDeepDecl` on `too_deep` — never
-- publish `<error>` silently, which would let `check A B` exit 0 and give C
-- — a valid use — two INTERNAL ERRORs at `C.beni:15:23` (an evidence
-- miscount). Expected: B's row goes through `Publisher.scheme`
-- and B reports NESTING TOO DEEP (the position is open: §14.1 does not yet
-- say which region a row's failure names), and C, reading a poisoned row,
-- says nothing. Oracle twin: at 508 tuples the program checks.
pub type Box a
    = Box a


